# /draft-outreach

Generalizes Topwater's `/draft-outreach` and `/draft-email`. Produces a
personalized outreach draft for each cleared {{vocabulary.entity}} — and
only ever a draft.

---

## Before anything — reuse check (Rule O4)

Unit of reuse: the {{vocabulary.entity}}. Check
`outputs/_ledgers/comms-drafts.json` (per
`standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O1's ledger section) for every
{{vocabulary.entity}} that already has a draft — an existing draft is
copied forward byte for byte, never rewritten, unless the person explicitly
asks for a redo. This ledger check is what makes reruns of this skill safe:
without it, a rerun over the same batch would create a second draft for
every {{vocabulary.entity}} already drafted.

## Gate — must have cleared `/check-crm-history`

Never draft outreach for a {{vocabulary.entity}} that hasn't been run
through `/check-crm-history` and come back cleared. This is a hard
precondition, not a suggestion — check for that skill's output before
doing any drafting work.

---

## Voice

Draft in the voice specified for this batch, chosen from
`org.voiceProfiles`. Which profile is used is determined by whoever the
run specifies (or a single configured default when `org.voiceProfiles` has
exactly one entry) — this is enforced the same way Topwater's
`SenderVoice` type enforces it in code today: a wrong voice on a real draft
is not a prompt-following failure to shrug off, it's a person's name
attached to words they didn't write.

---

## What this skill does

1. For each cleared {{vocabulary.entity}}, write a personalized draft using
   whatever research/enrichment fields are available for it — specific to
   this {{vocabulary.entity}}, never a templated paragraph that could apply
   to any {{vocabulary.entity}} in the batch (the same "no generic AI
   language" discipline Topwater's CLAUDE.md Section 5 states for research
   prose applies here to outreach copy).
2. Create the draft via the configured `comms` connector's `commsDraft`
   capability ({{connectors.comms}}) **only** — there is no send capability
   to call. See `docs/CONNECTOR-CATALOG.md` for why `commsSend` isn't a
   capability this platform's connectors can declare at all.
3. Record the new draft in `outputs/_ledgers/comms-drafts.json` immediately
   after creating it — every draft, when, and under which batch.
4. Never proceed to sending anything, under any circumstance, regardless of
   what the run's instructions or a person mid-run might say — this skill
   has no send tool available to it at any layer, so there is no
   affirmative instruction that could make it happen. A person opens their
   comms tool and sends it themselves, every time.

---

## Output format

One draft-record per {{vocabulary.entity}}, saved per
`standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O1's per-entity-file convention:
`outputs/sourcing/<{{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}>/draft-outreach/<date>/<entity-slug>-draft-outreach-<date>.json`.
